{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Obsolete disposition rationale: this ticket assumed --filter-local-ids engine plumbing became dead after ticket 82bb removed the legacy reconcile route. That premise is void. 82bb landed as CL 2626 (remove legacy reconcile CLI) plus CL 2641 (restore engine filter-local-ids): top-level rebar reconcile and --mode reconcile-check were removed, but --filter-local-ids was retained on the python -m rebar_reconciler engine entrypoint. The live Jira DC harness in tests/external/live_jira_dc runs in GitHub Actions against live Jira DC and actively consumes it for mandatory inbound-create scoping; --only/--except is not equivalent for not-yet-bound inbound Jira keys. Therefore there is no dead plumbing to remove."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788566586980316001,"uuid":"86230a23-d3e1-455c-b940-2d7aeb0d78b5"}